WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.410
- [Mark] Okay, Alicia.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.410
- Hello.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.280
- [Mark] Where are you from originally?

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.870
- [Alicia] I'm originally
from Alma, Michigan.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.918
- [Mark] Alma, Michigan? Where's that?

00:00:13.918 --> 00:00:14.751
- [Alicia] Yeah,

00:00:14.751 --> 00:00:16.170
it's like right in the center
of the state of Michigan.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.102
- [Mark] Oh okay, I'm from Detroit.

00:00:17.102 --> 00:00:18.650
- [Alicia] Oh okay, I'm
from like Central Michigan?

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.110
Yeah so, that's where I'm from.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.327
- [Mark] Welcome to LA.

00:00:22.327 --> 00:00:23.160
- Thank you.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.068
- [Mark] How long you been here?

00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:25.471
- I've been here this time nine months.

00:00:25.471 --> 00:00:26.304
- [Mark] Oh, you're new.

00:00:26.304 --> 00:00:27.386
- Yeah.

00:00:27.386 --> 00:00:28.770
- [Mark] What got you out here?

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.993
- I left my husband of 18 years,

00:00:30.993 --> 00:00:33.530
and we lived out here before,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.946
so it felt like the city
was just calling me,

00:00:35.946 --> 00:00:37.670
you know to come back.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.510
- [Mark] Why is that?

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.864
- I love this city, I love this city.

00:00:40.864 --> 00:00:42.170
I don't know why, but I do.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.960
- [Mark] You're in the, as they say,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.234
the asshole of the city
right now. (laughs)

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.434
- Yeah, the bottom of the bottom (laughs)

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.238
- [Mark] This is the garbage can.

00:00:50.238 --> 00:00:51.071
- Yep.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.180
- [Mark] So, let's start
with your childhood.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.490
Tell me how you grew up.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.275
What parents were like-

00:00:58.275 --> 00:00:59.390
- Yep, I had both parents
up until I was 11,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.420
and then my dad did some
stuff and he went to prison,

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.770
then my mom became a single mom,

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.780
and then life got a little hard, so.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.730
- [Mark] Why did your dad go to prison?

00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:11.180
- For molesting two of my friends.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.030
- [Mark] Oof.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.381
- Yeah, when I was 11 he made me watch,

00:01:14.381 --> 00:01:16.887
and there's just crazy
stuff that, you know...

00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:18.250
- [Mark] But you weren't molested?

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.430
- No.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.160
Nope, he didn't touch me or my sisters,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.632
I have two older sisters.

00:01:22.632 --> 00:01:23.977
- [Mark] But you had
to watch your friends-

00:01:23.977 --> 00:01:25.410
- I mean he might as well of-

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.162
- [Mark] That's almost worse, right?

00:01:27.162 --> 00:01:28.123
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:30.050
So, and that was in South Carolina,

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.800
and then we moved back to Michigan.

00:01:33.581 --> 00:01:34.702
- [Mark] That's hard.

00:01:34.702 --> 00:01:35.840
- Yeah, yeah it was a little rough,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.832
especially comin' back when,
you know kids are mean,

00:01:37.832 --> 00:01:40.769
so when I came back they
already knew what was,

00:01:40.769 --> 00:01:43.430
small town talk you know, everybody,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.653
my dad was well-known in the town so,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.000
it made my life,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.750
I had to start fighting at that age

00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:51.905
to keep my head above water,

00:01:51.905 --> 00:01:53.900
so my life flipped around
from being innocent

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.723
to havin' to basically
grow up real quick at 11.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.320
- [Mark] And then
where'd it go from there?

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.623
- I got in a lot of trouble,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.510
became a delinquent basically,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.660
I'm the black sheep of
the family as it is,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.530
so like it just came
to be where, you know,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.970
me and my sisters,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.930
my oldest sister had her own
place because she had kids,

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.580
I became an aunt at 10 years old,

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.020
so she had her own place,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.240
my other sister lived with me,

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.740
and she became kinda like my mom,

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.140
because my mom was workin' two jobs,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.030
she was hardly ever home,

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.953
just to keep food and
house over our heads.

00:02:36.163 --> 00:02:38.570
I just went the other way,

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.120
you know fightin' and gettin' in trouble,

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.630
doing drugs, and that's
where I felt comfortable

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.770
after all this that happened,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:51.770
so I don't regret anything that's happened

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.040
because it's made me who I am today,

00:02:55.198 --> 00:02:57.110
but you know I wish I
could take some back but...

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.805
- [Mark] Do you have kids of your own?

00:02:58.805 --> 00:02:59.797
- Yeah, I have five.

00:02:59.797 --> 00:03:00.630
- [Mark] Five?

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.463
And what ages?

00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:04.463
- I have an 18, a 17, a 14, a 13, and 10.

00:03:05.331 --> 00:03:06.850
- [Mark] And where are they now?

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.480
- My oldest three live with my mom,

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.680
and my youngest two live with their dad,

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.686
my husband that I just left.

00:03:13.686 --> 00:03:17.890
- [Mark] So you're out
here living on the street,

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:18.723
or are you...

00:03:18.723 --> 00:03:19.723
- I'm in a tent, yeah.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.580
Somebody stole all of my identification

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.460
when I first got here,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.980
so and I'm from out of state,

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.710
so it's really hard to get
my identification back.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.098
- [Mark] That's terrible.

00:03:30.098 --> 00:03:30.988
- Yeah.

00:03:30.988 --> 00:03:32.712
- [Mark] People get
stuff stolen every day.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.545
- Yeah, I don't know,

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.548
I think I've been through like 30 tents

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.890
since I've been here,

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.683
replaced clothing numerous times,

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.080
it's just, it's crazy out here.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.180
They'll take anything they think is value.

00:03:48.774 --> 00:03:50.600
- [Mark] And so what's your drug?

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.003
- I dib and dabble with
cocaine, crack cocaine.

00:03:55.003 --> 00:03:55.870
- [Mark] Just crack?

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:56.703
- Yeah.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.533
And weed, I smoke weed.

00:03:58.533 --> 00:03:59.450
- [Mark] How long you been doin' crack?

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.525
- On and off for about 18 years almost.

00:04:01.525 --> 00:04:03.198
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:04:03.198 --> 00:04:04.031
- Yeah.

00:04:04.031 --> 00:04:04.864
- [Mark] So while you were
having kids and everything?

00:04:04.864 --> 00:04:06.060
- Yeah, I stopped when I was having kids,

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.890
and then you know...

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:09.723
- [Mark] Got back on.

00:04:09.723 --> 00:04:11.091
- Things just...

00:04:11.091 --> 00:04:13.233
Just didn't go as planned.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.970
- [Mark] So you've been clean for a time?

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:21.010
- Oh yeah, I've been clean
for a length of time,

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:24.030
you know 10 months
here, nine months there,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.513
couple years here, you know,

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.020
other than that I've
always went back to it.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.370
Even though I can maintain a life,

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.030
it's not that I can't maintain my life,

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.423
it's just, you know I'm
a functioning addict,

00:04:36.593 --> 00:04:37.570
that's what they'd call it.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.860
I know I have a problem,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.890
I know I do.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:40.803
It's just,

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.980
right now, I don't care to deal with it,

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:45.973
to be quite honest.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:51.214
I was, I mean I was with
my husband from 18 to 36,

00:04:51.214 --> 00:04:53.693
my birthday's in a couple weeks too,

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.230
I didn't really have my
life, you know what I mean?

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:02.803
It was like I was a mom and
a wife from the age of 18,

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.040
I didn't get to have this,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.860
so I'm like taking me now,

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:09.940
you know for a minute,

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.160
so that's what I'm trying to do

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.110
is just do me and find out who I am.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.191
- [Mark] So are you still
in contact with your kids?

00:05:16.191 --> 00:05:19.206
- [Alicia] I haven't talked
to them in a couple months,

00:05:19.206 --> 00:05:21.082
but you know me and my husband
are still good friends,

00:05:21.082 --> 00:05:24.643
we're not on bad terms at all.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.048
- [Mark] Are your parents around?

00:05:29.048 --> 00:05:31.210
- [Alicia] I haven't spoken
to my parents in 10 years,

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.560
since my youngest was born.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.220
We had a lot of fall outs,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.950
my mom and dad didn't like my husband,

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.330
they feel like because
he was older than me

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.900
that he, you know, took me away from them,

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.690
and influenced me into getting into drugs.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:44.523
Nobody influenced me,

00:05:44.523 --> 00:05:45.700
I mean yeah, granted he did it,

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.510
but I chose to do it you know what I mean,

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.860
I don't blame him for that.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.970
But the drugs caused me to

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.510
sign rights over to my
oldest three to my mom,

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.223
because of the things we were
going through at the time.

00:06:01.629 --> 00:06:03.829
But my husband is the
father of all my kids.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.486
- [Mark] And what do you
do for money out here?

00:06:10.486 --> 00:06:12.940
- Uh I do...
- What a lot of the girls do?

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:13.773
Yeah.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.790
It's taken care of me for nine months,

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:17.900
I haven't had to rely on,

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.990
and you know I never had a pimp,

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.637
I always tell 'em I'm my own pimp,

00:06:21.637 --> 00:06:23.590
I take care of myself,

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.410
I say what I want to do
when I want to do it,

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.060
not nobody tellin' me what to do,

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.753
and thank God,

00:06:28.753 --> 00:06:30.340
by the grace of God,

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.820
nobody's tried to force me to do,

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.880
no pimp or anything like that around here,

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.263
you know they've all, they
respect me for what I do.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.880
I don't think what I do defines me though,

00:06:45.123 --> 00:06:47.020
because if I had my ID,

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:47.860
I'd have a job.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.413
I'd rather work than do this,

00:06:50.416 --> 00:06:51.966
but it's quick money right now.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.163
Unfortunately.

00:06:55.998 --> 00:06:58.430
- [Mark] What do you have
planned for the next five years?

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.580
- I'm hoping to have a
place with my kids out here,

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.423
that's my goal.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.343
And to have a nice job.

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:09.379
- [Mark] And to get clean.
- And get clean, for sure,

00:07:09.379 --> 00:07:10.483
that'd be the first, you know.

00:07:10.483 --> 00:07:12.149
If I wasn't down here, I
probably wouldn't be doin' it,

00:07:13.323 --> 00:07:15.293
because there's so much
other things here to do,

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:19.440
than our small towns that we've lived in.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.850
I've lived all across this country though,

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:21.683
me and my husband,

00:07:21.683 --> 00:07:26.070
before we came out here in 2016,

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:30.380
we traveled the country with our kids,

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.000
my 13 and my 10 year old,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.683
so we've been up and down
the coasts, both coasts,

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.460
across, like I said, east
to west and south to north.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.250
We've been everywhere,

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.563
it's been an adventure.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.090
- [Mark] Good luck from here.
- [Alicia] Yeah, God's got me,

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:53.003
I know He does.

00:07:53.911 --> 00:07:54.744
He's got a better life for me,

00:07:54.744 --> 00:07:56.570
He had me come out here for a reason,

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.270
and I've always wanted to be,

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.540
not so much a drug counselor,

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.310
but to help people that
are on the streets,

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.170
and, you know, because I've
been in their predicament,

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:08.560
so I know what it takes to get out of it,

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.743
if that makes sense.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.163
And hopefully my story can touch somebody.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.000
Because I've been through a lot,

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.840
I don't look like it, I
carry myself very well,

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.483
but whew, it's been a life.

00:08:22.345 --> 00:08:25.130
- [Mark] Thank you for sharing your story.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.333
- No problem, thank you.

